WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.467 --> 00:00:02.602
Who leaked them. Why were they leaked?

00:00:02.602 --> 00:00:04.270
How many secrets were lost?

00:00:04.270 --> 00:00:05.572
These are the key new questions

00:00:05.572 --> 00:00:06.473
this morning.

00:00:06.473 --> 00:00:07.841
As the Pentagon scrambles

00:00:07.841 --> 00:00:08.908
to do damage control

00:00:08.908 --> 00:00:10.877
after a highly classified documents

00:00:10.877 --> 00:00:12.245
surfaced online.

00:00:12.245 --> 00:00:14.748
CNN has reviewed 53 of these documents.

00:00:14.981 --> 00:00:16.716
All of them appear to have been produced

00:00:16.716 --> 00:00:19.352
between mid-February and early March.

00:00:19.619 --> 00:00:20.987
Some reveal how the U.S.

00:00:20.987 --> 00:00:22.255
has been eavesdropping on

00:00:22.255 --> 00:00:23.623
key allies, including

00:00:23.623 --> 00:00:26.092
South Korea, Israel, Ukraine.

00:00:26.092 --> 00:00:27.293
A source close to Ukrainian

00:00:27.293 --> 00:00:29.262
President Volodymyr Zelensky tells CNN.

00:00:29.262 --> 00:00:30.997
Ukraine has already altered

00:00:30.997 --> 00:00:32.732
some of its military plans

00:00:32.732 --> 00:00:34.868
because of these leaks.

00:00:34.868 --> 00:00:36.503
CNN national security reporter

00:00:36.503 --> 00:00:38.071
Tasha Bertrand joins us now

00:00:38.071 --> 00:00:39.806
live from the Pentagon to Tasha,

00:00:39.806 --> 00:00:40.774
what are you learning about

00:00:40.774 --> 00:00:42.842
where these documents came from

00:00:42.842 --> 00:00:46.179
and how the administration is responding

00:00:46.479 --> 00:00:47.814
John, it's really remarkable.

00:00:47.814 --> 00:00:48.581
What we are learning

00:00:48.581 --> 00:00:49.682
is that these documents

00:00:49.682 --> 00:00:50.683
first appeared

00:00:50.683 --> 00:00:51.584
on a social media

00:00:51.584 --> 00:00:53.553
platform called Discord Discord

00:00:53.553 --> 00:00:55.221
at least a month ago.

00:00:55.221 --> 00:00:56.856
And there are at least 50 of them,

00:00:56.856 --> 00:00:58.258
which CNN has reviewed,

00:00:58.258 --> 00:01:00.427
and all of them have classified markings,

00:01:00.427 --> 00:01:01.528
including some

00:01:01.528 --> 00:01:02.862
up to the top secret level,

00:01:02.862 --> 00:01:03.830
which is the highest level

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:05.799
of classification in the US government.

00:01:05.799 --> 00:01:06.266
Now.

00:01:06.332 --> 00:01:06.866
The US

00:01:06.866 --> 00:01:08.902
Department of Justice is investigating

00:01:08.902 --> 00:01:09.269
the matter

00:01:09.269 --> 00:01:11.204
based on a referral from the Pentagon,

00:01:11.204 --> 00:01:11.805
which referred

00:01:11.805 --> 00:01:13.473
the matter to the Justice Department

00:01:13.473 --> 00:01:15.575
and the FBI for further investigation

00:01:15.575 --> 00:01:16.776
on Friday night.

00:01:16.776 --> 00:01:18.344
But look, these documents contain

00:01:18.344 --> 00:01:20.146
incredibly sensitive information

00:01:20.146 --> 00:01:21.181
about Ukrainian troop

00:01:21.181 --> 00:01:22.882
movements, strengths and weaknesses,

00:01:22.882 --> 00:01:23.750
including weaknesses

00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:25.051
in their air defenses.

00:01:25.051 --> 00:01:26.553
As well as really important

00:01:26.553 --> 00:01:27.654
and new information

00:01:27.654 --> 00:01:29.456
about just how far the US

00:01:29.456 --> 00:01:30.290
intelligence community

00:01:30.290 --> 00:01:32.492
has been able to go in penetrating

00:01:32.492 --> 00:01:34.761
the Russian Defense Ministry as well.

00:01:34.961 --> 00:01:36.162
As the Russian mercenary

00:01:36.162 --> 00:01:37.530
organization Wagner Group,

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:37.997
which of course

00:01:37.997 --> 00:01:39.966
is also carrying out operations

00:01:39.966 --> 00:01:41.000
in Ukraine.

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:42.368
Now, we are also learning

00:01:42.368 --> 00:01:44.604
from these documents that this comes

00:01:44.804 --> 00:01:45.472
this information

00:01:45.472 --> 00:01:46.239
in these top secret

00:01:46.239 --> 00:01:47.974
documents come from a variety

00:01:47.974 --> 00:01:50.043
of different agencies across the U.S.

00:01:50.043 --> 00:01:50.443
government,

00:01:50.443 --> 00:01:52.045
including the CIA,

00:01:52.045 --> 00:01:52.879
as well as the Defense

00:01:52.879 --> 00:01:54.414
Intelligence Agency.

00:01:54.414 --> 00:01:56.349
And so this really has

00:01:56.349 --> 00:01:58.351
impacted a lot of different agencies

00:01:58.351 --> 00:01:59.486
across the government,

00:01:59.486 --> 00:02:01.387
as well as many of the United States,

00:02:01.387 --> 00:02:02.021
its closest

00:02:02.021 --> 00:02:04.691
allies, including Israel and South Korea.

00:02:04.724 --> 00:02:06.526
A lot of these documents detail U.S.

00:02:06.526 --> 00:02:07.560
eavesdropping

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:08.261
and intercepted

00:02:08.261 --> 00:02:10.363
communications of these foreign allies

00:02:10.497 --> 00:02:11.564
talking to each other.

00:02:11.564 --> 00:02:12.198
So obviously,

00:02:12.198 --> 00:02:13.466
there's going to be some friction here

00:02:13.466 --> 00:02:14.634
moving forward between the U.S.

00:02:14.634 --> 00:02:15.335
and allies.

00:02:15.335 --> 00:02:16.503
They are already, though,

00:02:16.503 --> 00:02:17.570
talking to those allies

00:02:17.570 --> 00:02:18.938
and conducting a damage assessment,

00:02:18.938 --> 00:02:21.207
John, of how this leak may impact

00:02:21.207 --> 00:02:22.542
national security.

00:02:22.542 --> 00:02:24.310
Natasha Bertrand, extraordinary stuff.

00:02:24.310 --> 00:02:24.978
Thank you so much.

00:02:24.978 --> 00:02:26.146
Keep us posted.

00:02:26.146 --> 00:02:26.513
And Kate,

00:02:26.513 --> 00:02:27.313
I have to believe

00:02:27.313 --> 00:02:28.581
there's a great deal of concern

00:02:28.581 --> 00:02:29.649
because the leaker

00:02:29.649 --> 00:02:30.750
could still be out there.

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:31.551
That's exactly right.

00:02:31.551 --> 00:02:31.751
And you're

00:02:31.751 --> 00:02:33.520
talking about kind of the scope of where

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:34.787
this leaked information came from.

00:02:34.787 --> 00:02:36.656
Let's dig into a little bit more of what

00:02:36.656 --> 00:02:37.857
what is being revealed

00:02:37.857 --> 00:02:38.925
in these documents.

00:02:38.925 --> 00:02:40.426
Many of the leaked documents,

00:02:40.426 --> 00:02:41.694
as Natasha was talking about,

00:02:41.694 --> 00:02:43.396
deal with Russia's war

00:02:43.396 --> 00:02:44.130
on Ukraine,

00:02:44.130 --> 00:02:47.000
including intelligence on both countries.

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:48.801
One secret document from February.

00:02:48.801 --> 00:02:51.004
Details the diminishing missile stocks

00:02:51.271 --> 00:02:52.772
that Ukraine has on hand

00:02:52.772 --> 00:02:55.041
and also includes estimated delivery

00:02:55.241 --> 00:02:57.343
of additional weapons systems

00:02:57.343 --> 00:02:58.645
and the training plans

00:02:58.645 --> 00:03:00.880
for Ukrainian soldiers on those systems.

00:03:01.181 --> 00:03:02.849
Now, another document shows proposed

00:03:02.849 --> 00:03:04.150
military strategies

00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:05.718
for Ukraine, logistics

00:03:05.718 --> 00:03:07.620
and policy recommendations

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:09.522
for the country, for Ukraine.

00:03:09.522 --> 00:03:10.623
Yet another document

00:03:10.623 --> 00:03:12.091
and it's marked top secret.

00:03:12.091 --> 00:03:14.360
It contains information on Russia

00:03:14.494 --> 00:03:16.629
and Ukrainian battalion sizes

00:03:16.629 --> 00:03:17.730
and their locations,

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:19.566
as well as the level of battlefield

00:03:19.566 --> 00:03:22.435
casualties being suffered on both sides.

00:03:22.702 --> 00:03:23.002
U.S.

00:03:23.002 --> 00:03:24.304
officials believe that the losses

00:03:24.304 --> 00:03:26.139
spelled out in this document

00:03:26.139 --> 00:03:27.173
in particular

00:03:27.173 --> 00:03:28.208
may have been altered

00:03:28.208 --> 00:03:30.343
to show fewer Russian casualties

00:03:30.577 --> 00:03:31.711
than estimated.

00:03:31.711 --> 00:03:33.580
Other documents show the extent of U.S.

00:03:33.580 --> 00:03:34.681
spying operations

00:03:34.681 --> 00:03:35.882
on South Korea

00:03:35.882 --> 00:03:36.649
and Israel,

00:03:36.649 --> 00:03:38.885
including with relation to South Korea.

00:03:38.885 --> 00:03:42.055
A conversation between two senior South

00:03:42.055 --> 00:03:43.723
Korean national security officials

00:03:43.723 --> 00:03:45.858
about their concerns over a U.S.

00:03:45.858 --> 00:03:47.327
request for ammunition

00:03:47.327 --> 00:03:48.928
that would be sent to Ukraine.

00:03:48.928 --> 00:03:50.597
Those officials discuss a way

00:03:50.597 --> 00:03:52.198
to get around the country's

00:03:52.198 --> 00:03:53.833
policy of not supplying

00:03:53.833 --> 00:03:56.302
lethal aid to countries at war.

00:03:56.502 --> 00:03:57.870
And when it comes to Israel.

00:03:57.870 --> 00:03:59.172
Some of those leaked documents

00:03:59.172 --> 00:04:00.773
have sparked outrage in the country.

00:04:00.773 --> 00:04:02.709
Intelligence gathered allegedly

00:04:02.709 --> 00:04:03.843
revealing that Israel's

00:04:03.843 --> 00:04:05.945
own intelligence service from Assad

00:04:05.945 --> 00:04:07.647
has been encouraging protests

00:04:07.647 --> 00:04:09.616
against the country's new government.

00:04:09.616 --> 00:04:10.883
The prime minister's office

00:04:10.883 --> 00:04:13.286
has already come out and flatly denied

00:04:13.486 --> 00:04:14.587
that assessment.

00:04:14.587 --> 00:04:16.322
Now, joining me, there's a lot in here,

00:04:16.322 --> 00:04:17.624
but joining me for much more on

00:04:17.624 --> 00:04:19.592
this is Lieutenant General Mark Hertling.

00:04:19.592 --> 00:04:21.728
Mark Hertling, CNN, military analyst.

00:04:21.728 --> 00:04:22.262
General,

00:04:22.262 --> 00:04:22.862
we lay out

00:04:22.862 --> 00:04:25.131
just some of what is being revealed

00:04:25.265 --> 00:04:26.399
in these documents.

00:04:26.399 --> 00:04:27.867
What's most problematic

00:04:27.867 --> 00:04:30.637
about these leaks from your view?

00:04:30.637 --> 00:04:33.573
Is what you said just a minute ago, Kate,

00:04:33.606 --> 00:04:34.674
is most problematic.

00:04:34.674 --> 00:04:36.042
There's a lot of them

00:04:36.042 --> 00:04:37.710
and they're across the board.

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:38.945
But what also adds to it,

00:04:38.945 --> 00:04:40.513
it's different than past leaks.

00:04:40.513 --> 00:04:41.447
Which have been,

00:04:41.447 --> 00:04:41.748
you know,

00:04:41.748 --> 00:04:43.516
documents like the Snowden leaks

00:04:43.516 --> 00:04:44.984
that we the WikiLeaks

00:04:44.984 --> 00:04:46.352
that are documented,

00:04:46.352 --> 00:04:48.988
pieces of paper that did tell the story.

00:04:49.289 --> 00:04:50.390
What these do

00:04:50.390 --> 00:04:52.425
and what we've seen some of them do

00:04:52.425 --> 00:04:53.459
or perhaps

00:04:53.459 --> 00:04:55.728
give misdirection or disinformation.

00:04:55.895 --> 00:04:57.230
They have been

00:04:57.263 --> 00:04:59.632
redesigned to show different things

00:04:59.799 --> 00:05:01.200
from the original documents.

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:02.535
We know that already.

00:05:02.535 --> 00:05:05.271
So it's a combination of real live data,

00:05:05.471 --> 00:05:06.105
real life

00:05:06.105 --> 00:05:08.207
secrets, as Natasha Bertrand said,

00:05:08.241 --> 00:05:08.941
you said there.

00:05:08.941 --> 00:05:10.310
Some of them are cops secret,

00:05:10.310 --> 00:05:11.811
but on some of those documents.

00:05:11.811 --> 00:05:13.279
So it's a top secret.

00:05:13.279 --> 00:05:14.247
No foreign,

00:05:14.247 --> 00:05:15.114
which means there

00:05:15.114 --> 00:05:16.883
is no foreign dissemination.

00:05:16.883 --> 00:05:17.984
That's the marking

00:05:17.984 --> 00:05:19.218
that's at the top of those.

00:05:19.218 --> 00:05:21.721
So it's not only the kind of intelligence

00:05:21.721 --> 00:05:23.156
we collect on phones,

00:05:23.156 --> 00:05:24.957
but also the kind of intelligence

00:05:24.957 --> 00:05:26.626
that all nations connect,

00:05:26.626 --> 00:05:28.161
collect on their friends to.

00:05:28.161 --> 00:05:30.330
We do this. Other nations do it too.

00:05:30.496 --> 00:05:32.065
But you don't like it to be

00:05:32.065 --> 00:05:33.700
put into the public space.

00:05:33.700 --> 00:05:34.500
You're hitting on something

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:35.501
that I wanted to ask you about,

00:05:35.501 --> 00:05:36.836
because if you're

00:05:36.836 --> 00:05:38.571
if we're putting in perspective, it's

00:05:38.571 --> 00:05:40.406
one thing if intelligence is leaked,

00:05:40.406 --> 00:05:41.074
never a good thing.

00:05:41.074 --> 00:05:42.442
But if intelligence is leaked

00:05:42.442 --> 00:05:44.811
about a past program or a broader

00:05:45.378 --> 00:05:47.080
strategy or operation,

00:05:47.080 --> 00:05:48.848
what we're looking at here in the sense

00:05:48.848 --> 00:05:49.682
that we're getting

00:05:49.682 --> 00:05:50.850
in the reaction to it is

00:05:50.850 --> 00:05:51.551
what does it mean

00:05:51.551 --> 00:05:53.419
when it's in real time, general,

00:05:53.419 --> 00:05:54.420
when the leak has to do

00:05:54.420 --> 00:05:55.355
with supply levels

00:05:55.355 --> 00:05:57.323
and capabilities in an ongoing war?

00:05:59.058 --> 00:05:59.859
Yeah, again, I'll

00:05:59.859 --> 00:06:01.227
compare it to the WikiLeaks

00:06:01.227 --> 00:06:03.029
a couple of years ago that occurred.

00:06:03.029 --> 00:06:04.263
Those were cables

00:06:04.263 --> 00:06:05.231
and things that were going on

00:06:05.231 --> 00:06:06.199
between embassies

00:06:06.199 --> 00:06:08.101
and had long term planning issues.

00:06:08.101 --> 00:06:10.136
But when you're talking about today,

00:06:10.603 --> 00:06:12.772
the Russian invasion in Ukraine,

00:06:12.939 --> 00:06:14.307
our intent

00:06:14.307 --> 00:06:17.009
to support our Ukrainian partners

00:06:17.009 --> 00:06:17.944
with equipment

00:06:17.944 --> 00:06:19.245
and with supplies

00:06:19.245 --> 00:06:21.314
the battle maps that are happening,

00:06:21.581 --> 00:06:22.982
you know, within the last week

00:06:22.982 --> 00:06:24.517
or the last couple of days,

00:06:24.517 --> 00:06:27.687
you know, those killed real live close in

00:06:28.855 --> 00:06:31.491
a timely intelligence to an enemy.

00:06:31.591 --> 00:06:33.393
And that's not good.

00:06:33.393 --> 00:06:34.861
It's unfortunate

00:06:34.861 --> 00:06:36.295
that this has happened this way.

00:06:36.295 --> 00:06:38.097
But it's also truthfully, Kate,

00:06:38.097 --> 00:06:39.966
being risk misread

00:06:39.966 --> 00:06:42.034
by many people who don't understand

00:06:42.034 --> 00:06:43.569
what's in those documents.

00:06:43.569 --> 00:06:45.772
And I'll say The New York Times

00:06:45.772 --> 00:06:47.039
did a piece yesterday

00:06:47.039 --> 00:06:47.940
where they literally

00:06:47.940 --> 00:06:50.376
put two slides from the Joint Staff

00:06:50.543 --> 00:06:51.778
within their article

00:06:51.778 --> 00:06:53.913
with no description of what it was.

00:06:53.913 --> 00:06:54.881
You know, when I read it,

00:06:54.881 --> 00:06:56.549
when I looked at the two slides,

00:06:56.549 --> 00:06:58.851
having been on the Joint Staff once

00:06:58.851 --> 00:07:00.987
I knew exactly what it was saying

00:07:00.987 --> 00:07:03.089
and it was not saying the same thing

00:07:03.089 --> 00:07:04.891
that was in the newspaper report.

00:07:04.891 --> 00:07:06.359
So you're going to get amateur

00:07:06.359 --> 00:07:07.460
intel analysis

00:07:07.460 --> 00:07:08.294
analyst

00:07:08.294 --> 00:07:09.996
saying things that just aren't true

00:07:09.996 --> 00:07:11.564
about some of these documents,

00:07:11.564 --> 00:07:12.665
but that doesn't

00:07:12.665 --> 00:07:15.435
decrease the the the fear factor

00:07:15.435 --> 00:07:16.969
that's involved in these things

00:07:16.969 --> 00:07:18.671
leaking to the general public.

00:07:18.671 --> 00:07:20.573
General, real quick, what does U.S.

00:07:20.573 --> 00:07:22.508
military need to be doing right now

00:07:22.508 --> 00:07:24.310
to mitigate the damage from that?

00:07:26.312 --> 00:07:26.913
Yeah, fine.

00:07:26.913 --> 00:07:28.448
Fine. Who leaked it, first of all?

00:07:28.448 --> 00:07:30.450
And they've done that by addressing it

00:07:30.450 --> 00:07:32.552
with the Department of Justice.

00:07:32.552 --> 00:07:35.221
But there's also some internal looks on

00:07:35.221 --> 00:07:36.856
how these things could have gotten out.

00:07:36.856 --> 00:07:38.191
I have some ideas, having

00:07:38.191 --> 00:07:39.258
worked in the Pentagon.

00:07:39.258 --> 00:07:40.460
What might have happened.

00:07:40.460 --> 00:07:41.294
But they also have

00:07:41.294 --> 00:07:43.329
to do really rapid assessments,

00:07:43.563 --> 00:07:44.530
not only the U.S.

00:07:44.530 --> 00:07:45.431
military,

00:07:45.431 --> 00:07:47.567
but also militaries around the world

00:07:47.567 --> 00:07:49.168
and governments around the world.

00:07:49.168 --> 00:07:50.970
They have to pull intel analysts

00:07:50.970 --> 00:07:52.638
off their normal job,

00:07:52.638 --> 00:07:54.507
which takes them away from what

00:07:54.507 --> 00:07:56.409
they would normally be doing and say,

00:07:56.409 --> 00:07:57.610
hey, what's the damage

00:07:57.610 --> 00:07:59.679
assessment of these things, linking

00:07:59.679 --> 00:08:00.780
what could happen?

00:08:00.780 --> 00:08:02.248
Because people see

00:08:02.248 --> 00:08:03.616
what's on these documents

00:08:03.616 --> 00:08:06.185
or know about the sources and methods

00:08:06.185 --> 00:08:07.954
all of those things are important

00:08:07.954 --> 00:08:09.121
and all those things are.

00:08:09.121 --> 00:08:11.157
This is obviously happening as we speak.

00:08:11.190 --> 00:08:12.124
General, thank you

00:08:12.124 --> 00:08:13.693
very, very much, Sarah.

